<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles de Menou d'Aulnay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1604–<a href="/years/1650">1650</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles de Menou d'Aulnay was a French governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>. A lieutenant of Isaac de Razilly, he took charge of much of the colony after Razilly's death in 1635 and fought a long civil war with his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-la-tour">Charles de La Tour</a>. In 1645 he captured La Tour's fort on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-john-river">Saint John River</a>. He drowned near Port-Royal in 1650.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-de-menou-daulnay.jpg" alt="Charles de Menou d'Aulnay" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_d%27Aulnay.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
